  Chael-Chael. Full terms: licenses/dsh-ascii-whales-LICENSE.
- The vendored ascii-sharks animation retains its original authorship and
  terms. The source snapshot used by dsh-ascii-whales did not carry a separate
  LICENSE. Neither that integration's MIT license nor this file grants a new
  license for the animation source. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- ascii-kanji-sharks: MIT, with the full license in
  vendor/ascii-kanji-sharks/LICENSE.
- SJ reasoning ring 0.1.4 and its derived integration: MIT, with the complete
  license in vendor/sj-reasoning-ring/LICENSE. Embedded icons retain their
  separate notices in vendor/sj-reasoning-ring/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- dsh-bottom-info-bar 1.26.0 account adapters and asynchronous ledger core:
  MIT, copyright (c) 2026 songoao25. Pinned source commit:
  684beceac85120824d82c713b83e0e3e77a0eb3f. Full terms are preserved in
  vendor/bottom-info-bar/LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; provenance and
  per-file SHA-256 hashes are in vendor/bottom-info-bar/SOURCE.json.
  The runtime also includes LICENSE.bottom-info-bar and
  SOURCE.bottom-info-bar.json under lib/info/.
- Bundled font subsets: SIL Open Font License 1.1, with the full terms and
  naming information under assets/fonts/.
- The 0.8.41 startup PixelWhale renderer/code-fill adaptation uses official
  DeepSeek Harness MIT source; full terms: licenses/deepseek-harness-LICENSE.
  Its original frame atlas is loaded from the user's existing DSH install
  and is not embedded in this package.
- The source-only QA fixture includes CSS from DeepSeek Harness under the
  upstream MIT license, retained in qa/native-LICENSE.txt.

New standalone integration glue, settings UI, tests and documentation are
